<style>
  /* ── Split Button ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cf-split-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: stretch;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-purple-50, #5b5bd6);
    border-radius: var(--round-corners-corner_radius_sm, 4px);
    overflow: visible;
    position: relative;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__main {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-purple-50, #5b5bd6);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: var(--round-corners-corner_radius_sm, 4px) 0 0
      var(--round-corners-corner_radius_sm, 4px);
    transition: background 0.15s ease;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__label {
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__main:hover {
    background: var(--color-purple-10, #ebebf9);
  }

  .cf-split-btn__sparkle {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    height: 14px;
  }

  /* Light mode (default): show the light-fill icon, hide the dark-fill icon. */
  .cf-split-btn__sparkle[data-theme-icon='dark'] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Dark mode: show the dark-fill icon, hide the light-fill icon. */
  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__sparkle[data-theme-icon='light'] {
    display: none;
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__sparkle[data-theme-icon='dark'] {
    display: inline;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__divider {
    width: 1.5px;
    background: var(--color-purple-50, #5b5bd6);
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__chevron {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 8px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-purple-50, #5b5bd6);
    cursor: pointer;
    border-radius: 0 var(--round-corners-corner_radius_sm, 4px)
      var(--round-corners-corner_radius_sm, 4px) 0;
    transition: background 0.15s ease;
  }

  .cf-split-btn__chevron:hover {
    background: var(--color-purple-10, #ebebf9);
  }

  .cf-split-btn__chevron-icon {
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  /* Open state */
  .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-btn__chevron-icon {
    transform: rotate(-180deg);
  }

  .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-btn__main,
  .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-btn__chevron {
    background: var(--color-purple-10, #ebebf9);
  }

  /* ── Dropdown ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .cf-split-dropdown {
    display: none;
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(100% + 5px);
    min-width: 220px;
    background: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow:
      0 4px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1),
      0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    z-index: 200;
    padding: 6px 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--cf-border-subtle, #e8e8f0);
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown--right {
    right: 0;
    left: auto;
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown--left {
    left: 0;
    right: auto;
  }

  /* Mobile only (not tablet): flip the dropdown to open left, regardless of
     the "align" option passed to the component. */
  @media (max-width: 832px) {
    .cf-split-dropdown--right {
      right: auto;
      left: 0;
    }
  }

  /* Triangle pointer */
  .cf-split-dropdown__arrow {
    position: absolute;
    top: -2px;
    right: 20px;
    width: 12px;
    height: 7px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown__arrow::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%) rotate(45deg);
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    background: var(--cf-surface-02);
    border: 1px solid var(--cf-border-subtle);
    border-bottom: none;
    border-right: none;
  }

  .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-dropdown {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Dropdown items */
  .cf-split-dropdown__item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.12s ease;
    font-family: inherit;
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown__item:hover {
    background: var(--cf-surface-02, #f5f5fa);
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown__item:not(:last-child) {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cf-border-subtle, #f0f0f8);
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown__item-icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--cf-text-secondary, #4a4a5a);
  }

  .cf-split-dropdown__item-text {
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--cf-text-primary, #191924);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Dark mode */
  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn {
    border-color: var(--color-purple-40, #7878dc);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__main {
    color: var(--color-purple-30, #9898e0);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__divider {
    background: var(--color-purple-40, #7878dc);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__chevron {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-purple-30, #9898e0);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__chevron:hover {
    background: var(--color-purple-90, #1e1e3a);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn__main:hover {
    background: var(--color-purple-90, #1e1e3a);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-btn__main,
  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open .cf-split-btn__chevron {
    background: var(--color-purple-90, #1e1e3a);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown {
    background: var(--cf-surface-02, #1e1e2e);
    border-color: var(--cf-border-subtle, #2e2e40);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown__arrow::before {
    background: var(--cf-surface-02, #1e1e2e);
    border-color: var(--cf-border-subtle, #2e2e40);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown__item:hover {
    background: var(--cf-surface-03, #252535);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown__item:not(:last-child) {
    border-bottom-color: var(--cf-border-subtle, #2e2e40);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown__item-icon {
    color: var(--cf-text-secondary, #9090a8);
  }

  [data-theme='dark'] .cf-split-dropdown__item-text {
    color: var(--cf-text-primary, #e8e8f0);
  }

  /* Hidden state for page options */
  .hidden-page-options {
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>

<script>
  (function () {
    function getMdUrl() {
      var url = new URL(window.location.href);
      url.pathname = url.pathname.replace(/\.html$/, '.md');
      url.search = '';
      url.hash = '';
      return url.href;
    }

    var dropdownActions = {
      open_md: function (button, container) {
        window.open(getMdUrl(), '_blank');
      },

      copy_md: function (button, container) {
        var mdUrl = getMdUrl();
        var textSpan = button.querySelector('.cf-split-dropdown__item-text');
        var originalText = button.getAttribute('data-original-text');

        fetch(mdUrl)
          .then(function (response) {
            if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Failed to fetch MD file');
            return response.text();
          })
          .then(function (mdContent) {
            return navigator.clipboard.writeText(mdContent);
          })
          .then(function () {
            if (textSpan) {
              textSpan.textContent = 'Copied!';
              setTimeout(function () {
                textSpan.textContent = originalText;
              }, 2000);
            }
            container.classList.remove('cf-split-btn--open');
          })
          .catch(function (err) {
            console.error('Failed to copy MD content:', err);
            if (textSpan) {
              textSpan.textContent = 'Error';
              setTimeout(function () {
                textSpan.textContent = originalText;
              }, 2000);
            }
            container.classList.remove('cf-split-btn--open');
          });
      },

      ask: function (button, container) {
        var h1 = document.querySelector('.rst-content h1');
        var header;
        if (h1) {
          var clone = h1.cloneNode(true);
          var link = clone.querySelector('.headerlink');
          if (link) link.remove();
          header = clone.textContent.trim();
        } else {
          header = document.title.trim();
        }
        var prompt = 'Tell me about ' + header;
        if (window.docsAIAssistant && window.docsAIAssistant.open) {
          window.docsAIAssistant.open(prompt);
        }
      },
    };

    document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
      // Toggle chevron
      var chevron = event.target.closest('.cf-split-btn__chevron');
      if (chevron) {
        var container = chevron.closest('.cf-split-btn');
        var isOpen = container.classList.toggle('cf-split-btn--open');
        chevron.setAttribute('aria-expanded', isOpen ? 'true' : 'false');
        event.stopPropagation();
        return;
      }

      // Main ask button
      var main = event.target.closest('.cf-split-btn__main');
      if (main) {
        var container = main.closest('.cf-split-btn');
        dropdownActions.ask(main, container);
        event.stopPropagation();
        return;
      }

      // Dropdown menu item
      var menuItem = event.target.closest('.cf-split-dropdown__item');
      if (menuItem) {
        var container = menuItem.closest('.cf-split-btn');
        var action = menuItem.getAttribute('data-action');
        if (action && dropdownActions[action]) {
          dropdownActions[action](menuItem, container);
        }
        container.classList.remove('cf-split-btn--open');
        var chevronBtn = container.querySelector('.cf-split-btn__chevron');
        if (chevronBtn) chevronBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        return;
      }

      // Click outside — close all
      document.querySelectorAll('.cf-split-btn.cf-split-btn--open').forEach(function (btn) {
        btn.classList.remove('cf-split-btn--open');
        var chevronBtn = btn.querySelector('.cf-split-btn__chevron');
        if (chevronBtn) chevronBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      });
    });
  })();
</script>
                                
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="rst-content">
                    <div class="rst-inner">
                        <main
                            class="document"
                            itemscope="itemscope"
                            itemtype="http://schema.org/Article"
                        >
                            <article itemprop="articleBody" data-swiftype-index='true'>
                                
  <section id="manage-consumers-groups-using-c3">
<span id="controlcenter-userguide-consumers"></span><h1>Manage Consumers Groups Using Confluent Control Center<a class="headerlink" href="#manage-consumers-groups-using-c3" title="Link to this heading"></a></h1>
<p>Use <strong>Consumers</strong> to monitor consumer groups for all the topics in a cluster. <strong>Consumer lag</strong> enables you to monitor lag for consumers.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Considerations:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>Consumer lag for an individual topic can be accessed from the <a class="reference internal" href="../topics/view.html#c3-view-topic-consumer-lag"><span class="std std-ref">Topics</span></a> menu.</p></li>
<li><p><strong>Consumers</strong> is enabled by default using an access control setting in the Control Center properties files. For more information, see: <a class="reference internal" href="#c3-enable-disable-consumers"><span class="std std-ref">Enabling and disabling the Consumers feature</span></a></p></li>
<li><p><a class="reference internal" href="../security/c3-rbac.html#controlcenter-security-rbac"><span class="std std-ref">RBAC</span></a> takes precedence over access control settings.</p></li>
<li><p>If <a class="reference internal" href="../security/c3-rbac.html#controlcenter-security-rbac"><span class="std std-ref">RBAC</span></a> is enabled for Control Center, the resources you can access are determined by your assigned role or roles and their corresponding privileges.</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
<section id="manage-consumers-groups">
<span id="c3-all-consumers-groups"></span><h2>Manage consumers groups<a class="headerlink" href="#manage-consumers-groups" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<p>Use <strong>Consumer</strong> to manage and monitor consumers and consumer groups.</p>
<ul class="simple">
<li><p>View all consumer groups for a cluster</p></li>
<li><p>Search for a consumer group by ID</p></li>
<li><p>View the number of consumers and number of source topics for each consumer group</p></li>
<li><p>Set up a pre-populated alert for <a class="reference internal" href="../alerts/examples.html#consumer-lag-trigger"><span class="std std-ref">consumer lag</span></a></p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>To access Consumer</strong>:</p>
<ul class="simple">
<li><p>Select a cluster from the navigation bar and select <strong>Client</strong>, then select <strong>Consumers</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
</section>
<section id="monitor-consumer-lag">
<span id="c3-cg-view-consumer-lag"></span><h2>Monitor consumer lag<a class="headerlink" href="#monitor-consumer-lag" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<p>Use <strong>Consumer lag</strong> to monitor lag for consumers.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Considerations:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>The consumer group list displays information about your consumer groups, including the group ID, status, and protocol. You can also find values for group lag, and number of consumers, topics, and partitions.</p></li>
<li><p>Control Center limits the number of consumer groups shown in <strong>Consumer lag</strong> if there are many.</p></li>
<li><p>You can export consumer lag data as a CSV file.  For clusters with large amounts of data, you may see a placeholder value like <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">-999</span></code> in the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">currentOffset</span></code> field. This occurs because Control Center cannot display all the data immediately, and the offsets are not yet available. For large payloads, consider exporting consumer lag data using the Confluent CLI or Confluent Cloud APIs.</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
<p><strong>To monitor consumer lag</strong></p>
<ol class="arabic simple">
<li><p>Select your cluster name.</p></li>
<li><p>Choose <strong>Clients</strong> and select <strong>Consumer Lag</strong>. A list of consumer groups displays.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a consumer group from the list to see lag details for that group.</p></li>
</ol>
</section>
<section id="set-up-alerts-for-consumer-groups">
<span id="c3-cg-context-alert"></span><h2>Set up alerts for consumer groups<a class="headerlink" href="#set-up-alerts-for-consumer-groups" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<p>You can set alerts from the Consumer lag page. These options pre-populate most of
the consumer group trigger fields.</p>
<ul class="simple">
<li><p>On the Consumer lag page, click <strong>Set up an alert</strong>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p>For more details, see <a class="reference internal" href="../alerts/examples.html#consumer-lag-trigger"><span class="std std-ref">Consumer lag trigger</span></a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="enabling-and-disabling-the-consumers-feature">
<span id="c3-enable-disable-consumers"></span><h2>Enabling and disabling the Consumers feature<a class="headerlink" href="#enabling-and-disabling-the-consumers-feature" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<p><strong>Consumers</strong> is enabled by default.</p>
<p>You can disable by setting the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">confluent.controlcenter.consumers.view.enable</span></code> option in the Control Center
properties file to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">false</span></code>.  After disabling the feature, <strong>Consumer</strong> is no longer visible in Control Center.</p>
<p>To enable <strong>Consumers</strong> again, set the option back to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">true</span></code> and restart Control Center with the updated properties file.</p>
<p><strong>To disable Consumers</strong>:</p>
<ol class="arabic">
<li><p>In the <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">control-center.properties</span></code> file, set <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">confluent.controlcenter.consumers.view.enable</span></code> to <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">false</span></code>.</p>
<div class="highlight-bash notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>...
confluent.controlcenter.consumers.view.enable<span class="o">=</span><span class="nb">false</span>
...
</pre></div>
</div>
<p>Make the change in the appropriate Control Center properties files configured for your environments, including any of the following files:</p>
<ul class="simple">
<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">control-center-dev.properties</span></code></p></li>
<li><p><code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">control-center-production.properties</span></code></p></li>
</ul>
<p>Find the properties files here: <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">confluent-control-center/</span></code> For more information, see <a class="reference internal" href="../installation/properties.html#c3-properties-files"><span class="std std-ref">Control Center Configuration Examples for Confluent Platform</span></a>.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Restart Control Center and pass in the properties file for the configuration to take effect.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Local (dev) environment:</p>
<div class="highlight-bash notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>confluent<span class="w"> </span><span class="nb">local</span><span class="w"> </span>services<span class="w"> </span>control-center<span class="w"> </span>stop
confluent<span class="w"> </span><span class="nb">local</span><span class="w"> </span>services<span class="w"> </span>control-center<span class="w"> </span>start<span class="w"> </span>--config<span class="w"> </span>confluent-control-center/control-center.properties
</pre></div>
</div>
<div class="admonition important">
<p class="admonition-title">Important</p>
<p>Do not use <a class="reference external" href="https://docs.confluent.io/confluent-cli/current/command-reference/local/index.html">confluent local</a> for production use.</p>
</div>
</li>
<li><p>Production environment:</p>
<div class="highlight-bash notranslate"><div class="highlight"><pre><span></span>./bin/control-center-stop
./bin/control-center-start<span class="w"> </span>confluent-control-center/control-center.properties
</pre></div>
</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
</section>


                            </article>
